# Double standRiseAt(Int tick)
#
# How far the armour stand is off the ground on a given tick of the
# cutscene, in blocks. tick is measured from the start of the driver,
# which is also the tick shakeStand starts on.
#
# The lift is a triangle folded at riseTicks (up for the first half of
# 2 * riseTicks, down for the second) with smootherstep on each leg.
# smootherstep has zero first AND second derivative at both ends, so the
# stand eases in off the ground, eases out into the peak, eases in back
# down and eases out onto the floor. The fold's corner sits exactly where
# smootherstep's derivative is zero, so the peak comes out smooth rather
# than showing the kink.
#
# This is the single source of truth for the lift. shakeStand drives the
# stand with it, and moveBlockDisplays reads it to find where the stand
# WILL be when a display finishes interpolating, so the two can't drift
# apart. Ticks outside the run clamp to the ground.
#
# Folding is idempotent — standRiseAt(fold(t)) == standRiseAt(t) — so it
# is safe to call with a tick that has already been folded, which is what
# shakeStand does inside its loop.
@using irodoriAnimation
@fast

@define Int t = tick

@if t < 0
    @var t = 0
@fi
@if t > 2 * riseTicks
    @var t = 2 * riseTicks
@fi
@if t > riseTicks
    @var t = 2 * riseTicks - t
@fi

# smootherstep(u) = 6u^5 - 15u^4 + 10u^3, in Horner form.
@define Double u = Double(t) / Double(riseTicks)
@return standRise * u * u * u * (u * (u * 6D - 15D) + 10D)
